# SutonnyMJ (Bijoy Classic / ANSI) glyph table: source of truth for Classic output.
#
# This Source Code Form is subject to the terms of the Mozilla Public License, v. 2.0.
# If a copy of the MPL was not distributed with this file, You can obtain one at
# https://mozilla.org/MPL/2.0/.
# The mappings are derived from the Unicode->Bijoy table in converter.py of
# bijoy2unicode (https://github.com/Mad-FOX/bijoy2unicode), licensed under MPL-2.0.
# See THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md.
#
# Grammar (one row per line; '#' starts a comment):
#   <code point> [<code point>...]  ->  <byte> [<byte>...]  <source>
#
#   left   logical Unicode sequence (U+XXXX, up to 6) produced by the Bijoy composer
#   right  SutonnyMJ glyph bytes in Windows-1252 (hex). Classic output inserts the
#          Unicode equivalent of each byte (cp1252 decoding), e.g. 87 -> U+2021 for ে,
#          so the text round-trips through ANSI applications on code page 1252.
#   source verified  = rendered in the SutonnyMJ font and checked by eye
#          converter = taken from the Unicode->Bijoy table of the open-source converter
#                      github.com/Mad-FOX/bijoy2unicode (converter.py, main_char);
#                      NOT yet verified in the font. Rejected by --strict (release).
#
# Lookups are longest-match over the syllable's logical text. Visual reordering
# (pre-base kar first, reph glyph after its cluster) is done by the Classic backend, not
# by this table. One change from the converter: র + ্য uses ZWJ (U+200D), as the Unicode
# standard and the composer do, where the converter used ZWNJ.
#
# Known gap: ৳ (Shift+4) has no SutonnyMJ code in this table; Classic mode emits it
# unchanged until a verified code is found.

